  "query_preview": "..\nWhile a generally dry period remains through the weekend,\nprecipitable water remains between 1.75\" and 2.25\" across all\nislands. This moisture is expected to remain along with light and\nvariable winds, so island effect showers and isolated thunderstorms \nwill be possible Saturday, Sunday, and Monday. The highest chances\nwill be for Guam. Light northwesterlies Saturday across Guam may \nkeep showers more to the southeast. While no thunderstorms were\nobserved over the islands today, upper-level support looks to \nincrease slightly the next three days which should help support \nthunderstorm development. By Tuesday, westerlies winds ahead of a \nslowly developing trough will prevent further island effect showers, \nbut then bring additional monsoon moisture into the region by \nWednesday. This will bring shower coverage back to scattered with \nisolated thunderstorms possible. This trough will be closely \nmonitored for any potential impacts to the Marianas late next week.",
